        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cella is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European kelneh2, \"a small room\" (EtymDB 2.1), from a root for hiding seen in cēlō, \"to hide\" (Lewis & Short). English cell comes from it, and English hall is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
